You don’t want cluster-wide access, so use a Role (not ClusterRole).

# role-qa.yaml
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  namespace: qa
  name: qa-role
rules:
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["pods", "services", "configmaps"]
    verbs: ["get", "list", "watch", "create", "update", "delete"]
👉 This role allows CRUD operations on pods, services, and configmaps only inside qa namespace.

🔹 Step 6: Bind Role to QA User
